  "seminaryName": "Theological College",
  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "Winter is grey and indecisive, with one real snow that closes the federal government and none of the parishes.",
      "April is the blossoms and the tourists, and a week of weather so good it seems designed to be photographed.",
      "Summer is a swamp that the founders were warned about, and the collar is a wet ring by the end of the Gospel.",
      "October is the one month the city is beautiful without effort, and the whole diocese schedules its galas in it."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "Sunday in Georgetown is lawyers in blazers who could give the homily; Sunday in Anacostia runs long, and nobody looks at a watch.",
      "The Spanish Mass in the Maryland suburbs fills the hall and the lot, and the collection comes in small bills, carefully folded.",
      "Somebody with a security detail is at one of the Masses most weeks, and the ushers know which pew to leave empty."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The priests of Washington are careful talkers, because a remark at dinner can be a paragraph in a column by Wednesday.",
      "Half of them have a degree from the university and the other half have a theory about the ones who do.",
      "They know the nuncio's schedule better than their own, and they pretend, among themselves, not to."
    ]
  },
